---

<Layout
  title="Tipitaka Editions in Markdown"
  description="Digital reader showcasing canonical Pāḷi Tipiṭaka texts converted to Markdown across the tipitaka-md repositories: World Tipiṭaka Edition (WTK base), Pali Text Society (PTS), Buddha Jayanthi (BJT), Chaṭṭha Saṅgāyana (CST), and Royal Thai Edition (RTE)."
  lang="en"
>
  <main>
    <!-- Hero Banner -->
    <div class="hero-banner">
      <h1>Tipitaka Editions in Markdown</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Open Markdown Editions of the Complete Pāḷi Canon Across 5 International Traditions
        with Real-Time Variant Highlighting, Dictionary Lookup &amp; Direct Markdown Access
      </p>
      <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 1.5rem;">
        <a
          href="/reader.html?book=1V"
          class="btn-primary"
          style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; padding: 0.65rem 1.4rem; border-radius: 8px; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; color: #fff; background-color: var(--primary-color);"
        >
          <span>📖 Start Reading</span>
        </a>
        <a
          href="/guide.html"
          class="btn-secondary"
          style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; padding: 0.65rem 1.4rem; border-radius: 8px; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; border: 1px solid var(--border-color); color: var(--text-body); background-color: var(--bg-tertiary);"
        >
          <span>📘 Quick Guide</span>
        </a>
        <a
          href="/about.html"
          class="btn-secondary"
          style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; padding: 0.65rem 1.4rem; border-radius: 8px; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; border: 1px solid var(--border-color); color: var(--text-body); background-color: var(--bg-tertiary);"
        >
          <span>ℹ️ About</span>
        </a>
        <a
          href="#canon-directory"
          class="btn-secondary"
          style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; padding: 0.65rem 1.4rem; border-radius: 8px; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; border: 1px solid var(--border-color); color: var(--text-body); background-color: var(--bg-body);"
        >
          <span>📚 Browse Canon</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Project Overview -->
    <div class="home-intro-layout">
      <div>
        <p>
          <strong>Tipitaka Editions in Markdown</strong> is an open-access comparative reader for the
          entire Theravāda Buddhist Canon (<em>Tipiṭaka</em>) across five international editions
          converted into version-controlled <strong>Markdown format</strong>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Using <strong>The World Tipiṭaka Edition (WTK)</strong> as the
          canonical base text, the reader dynamically renders texts directly from the repositories,
          with instant links to <strong>view raw Markdown</strong>, <strong>download .md files</strong>,
          and explore on GitHub. Because the reader is dynamically constructed from what is
          currently in the repos, the site remains lightweight, fast, and does not need to be rebuilt
          when the underlying text files are updated.
        </p>
        <p>
          Textual variants between editions are highlighted dynamically:
        </p>

        <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 1.25rem 0;">
          <span class="legend-badge legend-add" style="padding: 0.4rem 0.8rem; font-size: 0.88rem; border-radius: 6px;">
            ● Addition: Word or phrase present in comparative edition
          </span>
          <span class="legend-badge legend-change" style="padding: 0.4rem 0.8rem; font-size: 0.88rem; border-radius: 6px;">
            ● Variant / Change: Orthographical or reading difference
          </span>
          <span class="legend-badge legend-del" style="padding: 0.4rem 0.8rem; font-size: 0.88rem; border-radius: 6px;">
            ● Omission: Word present in base edition omitted
          </span>
        </div>

        <p style="margin-bottom: 0;">
          The reader includes full <strong>Pāḷi grammar dictionary lookup</strong> on hover and tap,
          as well as dynamic transliteration between <strong>Roman (IAST)</strong>,
          <strong>Sinhala (සිංහල)</strong>, <strong>Thai (ไทย)</strong>,
          <strong>Burmese (မြန်မာ)</strong>, <strong>Devanagari (देवनागरी)</strong>, and <strong>Brahmi (𑀩𑁆𑀭𑀸𑀳𑁆𑀫𑀻)</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <figure class="home-volume-figure">
        <picture>
          <source type="image/webp" srcset="/images/tipitaka-volumes.webp" />
          <img
            src="/images/tipitaka-volumes.jpg"
