            <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap;">
              <span class="badge-code" style="font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700; color: #695d08; border-color: #695d08;">
                CST EDITION
              </span>
              <span style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">
                Source: <a href="https://github.com/VipassanaTech/tipitaka-xml" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: #695d08; text-decoration: underline;">VipassanaTech/tipitaka-xml ↗</a>
              </span>
            </div>
            <h2>🇲🇲 Chaṭṭha Saṅgāyana (CST)</h2>
            <p>
              Converted deterministically from the XML edition at <a href="https://github.com/VipassanaTech/tipitaka-xml" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: #695d08;">VipassanaTech/tipitaka-xml</a> (Vipassana Research Institute / VRI CST4, Sixth Buddhist Council text) across 217 books covering Mūla, Aṭṭhakathā, and Ṭīkā into structured Markdown with preserved footnotes and variant readings.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color); padding-top: 0.75rem; margin-top: auto; font-size: 0.85rem;">
            <a href="https://github.com/tipitaka-md/cst" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: #695d08; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none;">
              tipitaka-md/cst ↗
